    "taskType": "task1",
    "text": "The bar chart compares the proportions of commuters commuting by public transport in North and South in 2010, 2015 and 2020. All figures are expressed as percentages.\n\nOverall, the proportion in North decreased overall, whereas South increased overall. South recorded the higher figure at the end of the period. The difference between the regions narrowed, from 45 percentage points in 2010 to 30 points in 2020.\n\nIn North, the figure stood at 70% in 2010, before falling to 50% five years later. It then declined to 30% in 2020. The first interval saw a change of 20 percentage points, while the corresponding movement during the second half of the decade was 20 points.\n\nSouth followed a different pattern, starting at 25% and reaching 40% in 2015. By 2020, its figure was 60%. Comparing the two regions directly, North had the larger share at the beginning, while South led at the end. The final figures of 30% for North and 60% for South therefore show a gap of 30 percentage points.",
